WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys, it's Avengers week.
That's right.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm excited.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Avengers: Endgame"
is almost here,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.743
and I read that it could
make over a billion dollars

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.011 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in its first weekend.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.212 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:12.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
A billion dollars.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
That means after Thanos,
the Avengers' next big enemy

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.251 line:92%
is going to be Bernie Sanders.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Bernie Sanders ]
Tony Stark is in the 1%!

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
Speaking of Bernie Sanders,

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
last night
from 7:00 to midnight,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:30.730
CNN had five town halls
with five Democratic candidates.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, five straight hours
of town halls,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is why Wolf Blitzer
kicked off things by saying,

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Good evening.
I'm wearing a diaper."

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.606 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was weird.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the town halls
were pretty interesting.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take a look at the beginning
of Bernie's event.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
How about our first question?

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:50.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
We ready?
-Why not?

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why not, indeed.
-What else do we have to do?

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's actually
his campaign slogan.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Bernie 2020.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Bernie Sanders ] Why not?
What else do we have to do?

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why not?
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hurry up.
What else do we have to do?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.867 line:92%
[ Normal voice ] Hang on.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can we see Bernie
in that chair again?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.607 line:92%
Is that a town hall for Bernie,

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is that
"Weekend at Bernie's"?

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What?

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.080 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.718
But all the 2020 candidates
are on the campaign trail.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.920 line:92%
And a lot of them have to answer

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same questions
everywhere they go.

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:31.357
So to help everyone out,
we put together each candidate's

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.093 line:92%
most frequently asked questions.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.160 line:92%
They're kind of fascinating.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, first here
is Pete Buttigieg.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:39.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's most often asked,
"Are you lost, little boy?

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.400 line:92%
Where are your mommy and daddy?"

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. That's it?
-These are the most --

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the one
he's asked the most. Wow.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.173 line:92%
-Next, here's Cory Booker.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.241 line:92%
A lot of times he's asked,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When is the new
'Fast and Furious' coming out,

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.778 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Mr. Diesel?"

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.483 line:92%
Next up, here's Beto O'Rourke.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's most often asked,
"What kind of name is Beto?

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you named after
a rejected Avenger?"

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.956 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I am Beto!

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally,
here's Bernie Sanders.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.562 line:92%
He's most frequently asked,

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Were you mugged
on the way here,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.900 line:92%
or is that how you always look?"

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.835 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Get over here.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:18.204 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Give me your wallet."

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.172 line:92%
Oh, some business news here.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.242
After a rough couple of months,
Kraft Heinz announced

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're getting rid
of their CEO.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, and Heinz
is going to get him out

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.213 line:92%
the only way they know how --

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
flipping him upside down
and whacking him in the butt.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.751 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Grunting ]

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.823
At least they're not putting
a butter knife in his throat.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.094 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Guys, today is --

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, you've done it.
Come on, now.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today is William Shakespeare's
birthday.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.234 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So in honor of him...

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.938
I would like to recap some
of today's biggest news stories

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:54.240 line:92%
in the style of Shakespeare.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.241 size:81% position:41% line:92%
All right, here we go.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.244 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:03.216 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Slow music plays ]

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.293 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Mueller, oh, Mueller.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.428 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We doth see your report.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.530 line:92%
But alas, what does it all mean?

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
Republicans sayeth
it falls much too short,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
while Democrats sayeth,
"Yas, Queen."

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.972 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Avengers: Endgame"
is finally here.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Thanos is quite
the mean brute.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
But thine heroes approach,
so haveth no fear

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
as I say to myself,
"I am Groot."

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.822 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buttigieg, Beto, and Biden
and Bernie.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.295 line:92%
It's "B" after "B" in the race.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.832
But to Trump, 'tis no one
who seems too concerning.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just like,
"Let's go to space."

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.403 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:04.410
Kraft Heinz hath a new leader,
it seems, a CEO who's on the up.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's hope that the company
he can redeem

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the shadows
of thy Mayochup.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.785 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.956 size:81% position:41%
Elizabeth Warren says,
"Free school for all."

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
And methinks her idea
hath some legs.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
So come 2020,
head to class in the fall

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
and spend all of your money
on kegs.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you very much.
Thank you.

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.302 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:32.472 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wow.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wow.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.842 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wow.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I trained.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.
-I trained for years.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-My God.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.181 line:92%
-Ah. Listen to this, guys.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
A town in England
has been having problems

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
with aggressive seagulls
on its beaches,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:50.757
so they brought in a pair of
bald eagles to get rid of them.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:51.324 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's great.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now beachgoers
can relax in peace,

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing that if a seagull
gets too close,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:57.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
an eagle will swoop in
and murder it.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.531 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
The kids will never forget it.
[ Seagull squawks ]

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get this -- A pizza restaurant
in Texas was shut down

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:09.108
after people found out they were
putting laxatives in the pizza.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:10.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.444 line:92%
They even had a special deal.

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:15.114
If you're not on the toilet in
30 minutes, the next one's free.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

